  annotation = {中文辅助译名：用于问答的自然语言解释生成},
  abstract = {Large language models have achieved remarkable performance on various question answering (QA) tasks, but the explainability of their output remains challenging. To address this issue, recent work has proposed symbolic explanations called entailment trees as a way to explain and inspect a QA system’s answer. In order to improve the generation of such symbolic explanations and enhance the interpretability of the model, we introduce a new task called Question Answering Explanation Generation. This task retains the tree structure and maps symbols to natural language, aiming to generate natural language explanations from question-answer pairs. The advantage is that by generating natural language explanations, the reasoning process of the model becomes more explicit. Additionally, it abandons the requirement to precisely match relevant knowledge for all question-answer pairs, with only the question and answer considered as inputs. This makes the framework more general and applicable to real-world scenarios. Furthermore, we collected some question-answer data and used a bidirectional generation framework to construct a pseudo-dataset, which allows the model to gain a more comprehensive understanding of the association between QA and explanation. Moreover, we integrated context generation into the model’s generation process instead of providing the context directly as input to consider broader aspects and domain-specific knowledge relevant to the question and answer pair. Applying ou},
}

